@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Edit, local persistence and independent analysis pipelines
autonumber
actor Author
participant "WorkspaceCoordinator\nC#" as W
participant "ProjectRepository\nC# + glue" as Repo
participant "SourceAnalyzer\nRust worker" as Rust
participant "TeXEngineAdapter\nC++ worker" as TeX
participant "PdfEngineAdapter\nC++ worker" as PDF
Author -> W : edit file
W -> W : freeze project snapshot R
par local save (independent)
  W -> Repo : CommitAsync(R, expectedHead)
  Repo -> Repo : lock; verify blobs; IDB head transaction
  alt commit succeeds
    Repo --> W : saved R
  else quota / storage failure
    Repo --> W : typed failure; keep dirty R
  end
else source checks (independent)
  W -> Rust : analyzeSource(R, profile)
  Rust --> W : source report R
  W -> W : publish only if R still current
end
opt automatic compile enabled or explicit compile
  W -> W : verify selected engine / bundle readiness
  W -> TeX : compile(R, VFS, asset inventory)
  alt compilation succeeds
    TeX --> W : PDF artifact + logs + source map for R
    W -> PDF : inspectPdf(artifact R)
    PDF --> W : normalized facts for artifact R
    W -> Rust : analyzeCombined(R, profile, facts R)
    Rust --> W : combined report R
    W -> W : verify R / profile / artifact; publish
  else compile failed / missing asset
    TeX --> W : typed failure + compiler diagnostics
    W -> W : retain prior PDF labeled by revision
    W -> W : mark PDF checks for R unavailable
  end
end
note over W, PDF
A later edit creates R+1; stale R output cannot replace current diagnostics.
Coordinators delegate calls; native workers never call each other directly.
end note
@enduml
